---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../butterfly/butterfly.css";
---

<Base
  title="The Butterfly Effect"
  description="An interactive narrative where ordinary decisions lead to extraordinary consequences."
>
  <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/built">Things I've Built</a></p>
  <div id="butterfly"></div>

  <section class="section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <h2 id="about-title">About the experience</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The Butterfly Effect is a choice-driven story that starts on an ordinary morning. You are the person in it. The story does not assign you a gender, a job, or a history you didn’t choose.
      </p>
      <p>
        Small decisions change who trusts you, what you are allowed to know, and which morning you eventually reach. The page keeps that progress in this browser. It does not ask for an account, and it does not send your choices anywhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        A journal fills with what you have actually seen. After you finish a morning, a timeline map lets you look back at the routes you lived and return to an earlier moment without erasing the ending you already reached.
      </p>
      <p>
        The story includes psychological tension, grief, and situations that can feel distressing. There are no timers and no sound. You can change the type size, leave, and come back.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  import { mount } from "../butterfly/play.ts";

  const root = document.getElementById("butterfly");
  if (root) mount(root);
</script>
